{
  "$comment": [
    "PER-MACHINE Claude Code settings. Copy to `.claude/settings.local.json` (gitignored)",
    "and edit. Anything here is YOUR machine's choice and never reaches a fork or a /handoff.",
    "",
    "WHY plugins live here rather than in the committed settings.json (red-team R5, 2026-08-17):",
    "a marketplace entry pulls code from someone else's GitHub repository and runs it with the",
    "agent's full privileges in this repo -- the same privileges as the permission allowlist.",
    "`superpowers` is a third-party PERSONAL repository (obra/superpowers) and was previously",
    "auto-enabled in committed settings with no commit pin, so every fork inherited a",
    "third-party dependency it never chose, upstream changes flowed in silently, and /handoff",
    "shipped it to the receiving IT team as part of the package.",
    "",
    "Enabling it is a reasonable choice -- it is a genuinely useful plugin and the operator",
    "adopted it deliberately. It should just be a choice each fork makes knowingly.",
    "",
    "PIN IT if you enable it. A marketplace without a pin tracks its upstream default branch,",
    "so a compromised or simply changed upstream reaches you on the next session with no review.",
    "Claude Code resolves marketplace sources at install time; re-run `/plugin` after changing",
    "this file. Review what you are enabling first -- plugin code is not sandboxed from the repo."
  ],

  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "claude-code-plugins": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "anthropics/claude-code"
      }
    },
    "superpowers": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "obra/superpowers"
      }
    }
  },

  "enabledPlugins": {
    "frontend-design@claude-code-plugins": true,
    "superpowers@superpowers": true
  }
}
